{%- comment -%}
  Screens: VetPoints, rewards catalogue.

  data-spp-when="loyalty:ok" / "loyalty:error" are toggled by the controller's
  render() from state.loyalty.error — a failed ledger read (anything but an
  expired session, which signs the whole visit out instead) shows the error
  card below rather than a stale or fabricated balance. "loyaltyHistory:has" /
  "loyaltyHistory:empty" do the same for the transaction list. A brand-new
  customer with no ledger entry yet is not an error: they see a real zero.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%} ---------- VetPoints ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="spp__screen" data-spp-screen="loyalty" hidden aria-labelledby="spp-loy-h">
  <button type="button" class="spp__back" data-spp-go="dashboard">
    {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'chevron-left' %}Overview
  </button>

  {%- comment -%}
    One stacked column, full content width — matches the approved Claude
    Design mockup ("VetPets Portal V2") exactly: header, then the journey
    card, then reward history below it. Deliberately NOT the .spp__split
    two-column layout every other screen here uses; that mockup has no
    side column on this screen at any width.
  {%- endcomment -%}

  {%- comment -%} ---------- Ledger read failed ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="spp__card" data-spp-when="loyalty:error" hidden>
    <div class="spp__banner spp__banner--error" style="margin-bottom:0;">
      <span class="spp__banner-icon spp__banner-icon--error" style="width:26px;height:26px;font:700 15px/26px var(--spp-font);">!</span>
      <div>
        <div class="spp__banner-title">VetPoints is temporarily unavailable</div>
        <p>We couldn&rsquo;t load your balance just now. Your subscription and deliveries are not affected.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--secondary" style="margin-top:14px;min-height:48px;font-size:15px;" data-spp-act="retryLoyalty">
      <span data-spp-field="label.retryLoyalty">Try again</span>
    </button>
  </div>

  <div data-spp-when="loyalty:ok" hidden style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;">
    <div>
      <h1 class="spp__h1" id="spp-loy-h" style="margin-bottom:4px;">Your VetPoints</h1>
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:9px;font:700 44px/1.05 var(--spp-font);color:var(--spp-ink);letter-spacing:-0.03em;margin:6px 0 6px;">
        <span data-spp-field="loyalty.points">0</span>
        <span style="font:600 19px/1 var(--spp-font);color:var(--spp-body);">VetPoints</span>
      </div>
      <p style="margin:0;font:500 15px/1.45 var(--spp-font);color:var(--spp-body);">
        Earn <span data-spp-field="loyalty.perRenewal">100</span> VetPoints with every order.
      </p>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      The VetPoints journey — one node per founder-approved milestone, 200
      through 1,600. Achieved / current / locked state, and the connecting
      line's fill amount, are computed from the real balance alone (see the
      `milestones` list builder in assets/subscription-portal.js). Nothing
      here is redeemed or requested by the customer — every reward is
      issued automatically by the backend the moment its threshold is
      crossed. Rendered twice from the SAME data (see listData('milestones')
      in the controller): once into the desktop row below, once into the
      mobile vertical list — only one is ever visible at a time (CSS,
      1024px breakpoint), matching the mockup's own data-only split.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="spp__card spp__card--journey">
      <div class="spp__ms-head">
        <div style="min-width:0;">
          <span class="spp__ms-eyebrow">Milestone journey</span>
          <div class="spp__ms-next-name">Next reward: <span data-spp-field="loyalty.journeyNextName">Dental Chew Ball</span></div>
          <div class="spp__ms-next-meta" data-spp-field="loyalty.journeyNextMeta">Unlocks at 200 VetPoints</div>
        </div>
        <span class="spp__ms-counter" data-spp-field="loyalty.journeyCounter">0 / 200</span>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} Desktop: one full-width row, six columns. {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="spp__ms-row" data-spp-list="milestones">
        <template data-spp-tpl="milestones">
          <div class="spp__ms-col">
            <div class="spp__ms-flag">Next up</div>
            <div class="spp__ms-tile" data-spp-thumb><img data-spp-img alt=""></div>
            <div class="spp__ms-line">
              <span class="spp__ms-track spp__ms-track-a" data-spp-ms-track-a><span class="spp__ms-fill" data-spp-ms-fill-a></span></span>
              <span class="spp__ms-node" data-spp-ms-node></span>
              <span class="spp__ms-track spp__ms-track-b" data-spp-ms-track-b><span class="spp__ms-fill" data-spp-ms-fill-b></span></span>
            </div>
            <div class="spp__ms-pts" data-spp-field="ptsNumber">200</div>
            <div class="spp__ms-name" data-spp-field="name">Dental Chew Ball</div>
            <div class="spp__ms-sub" data-spp-field="sub">Locked</div>
          </div>
        </template>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} Mobile: the same nodes and line, stacked vertically. {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="spp__ms-vertical" data-spp-list="milestones">
        <template data-spp-tpl="milestones">
          <div class="spp__ms-vrow">
            <div class="spp__ms-vtrack">
              <span class="spp__ms-track spp__ms-track-a" data-spp-ms-track-a><span class="spp__ms-fill" data-spp-ms-fill-a></span></span>
              <span class="spp__ms-node" data-spp-ms-node></span>
              <span class="spp__ms-track spp__ms-track-b" data-spp-ms-track-b><span class="spp__ms-fill" data-spp-ms-fill-b></span></span>
            </div>
            <div class="spp__ms-vcard">
              <div class="spp__ms-vtile" data-spp-thumb><img data-spp-img alt=""></div>
              <div class="spp__ms-vbody">
                <div class="spp__ms-vtop">
                  <span class="spp__ms-vpts" data-spp-field="ptsNumber">200</span>
                  <span class="spp__ms-vsub" data-spp-field="sub">Locked</span>
                </div>
                <div class="spp__ms-vname" data-spp-field="name">Dental Chew Ball</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </template>
      </div>

      <div class="spp__ms-foot">
        <span class="spp__ms-foot-icon">
          {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'sparkle', size: 17 %}
        </span>
        <p>Your rewards are automatically added to your next delivery.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="spp__card">
      <h2 class="spp__h2" style="margin-bottom:8px;">Reward history</h2>
      <div data-spp-when="loyaltyHistory:has" hidden>
        <div data-spp-list="pointsHistory">
          <template data-spp-tpl="pointsHistory">
            <div class="spp__delivery" style="padding:12px 0;">
              <div style="flex:1;min-width:0;">
                <div class="spp__delivery-title" data-spp-field="label">Delivery renewed</div>
                <div class="spp__delivery-meta" data-spp-field="dateLong">10 July 2026</div>
              </div>
              <span style="font:700 14.5px/1 var(--spp-font);color:var(--spp-accent);" data-spp-field="delta">+100</span>
            </div>
          </template>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="spp__note" data-spp-when="loyaltyHistory:empty" hidden>
        No VetPoints activity yet &mdash; points appear here after your first renewal.
      </p>
      <p class="spp__info spp__info--dashed" style="margin-top:16px;padding:11px 13px;border-radius:12px;" data-spp-field="loyalty.disclosure"></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} ---------- Rewards catalogue ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="spp__screen" data-spp-screen="rewards" hidden aria-labelledby="spp-rew-h">
  <button type="button" class="spp__back" data-spp-go="loyalty">
    {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'chevron-left' %}VetPoints
  </button>

  <h1 class="spp__h1" id="spp-rew-h">Rewards catalogue</h1>
  <p class="spp__lede">
    <span data-spp-field="loyalty.points">0</span> points available.
    Redeemed rewards are added to your next delivery.
  </p>

  <div class="spp__grid" data-spp-list="rewards">
    <template data-spp-tpl="rewards">
      <div class="spp__card spp__card--sm" style="border-radius:18px;padding:16px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px;">
        <div style="display:flex;gap:13px;align-items:center;">
          <span class="spp__thumb spp__thumb--sm" data-spp-thumb><img data-spp-img alt=""></span>
          <div style="flex:1;min-width:0;">
            <div class="spp__media-title" data-spp-field="name">GloveWipes pack</div>
            <div style="font:600 13.5px/1.4 var(--spp-font);color:var(--spp-ink);margin-top:3px;">
              <span data-spp-field="cost">300</span> points
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        {%- comment -%}
          Requesting a reward reserves points and creates a pending_manual
          redemption. It never claims the reward has shipped.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <button type="button" class="spp__btn" style="min-height:46px;font-size:14.5px;" data-spp-act="requestRedemption" data-spp-reward>
          <span data-spp-field="btnLabel">Redeem</span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </template>
  </div>
</section>
